[s0l0!-header][h1]Nested if Statements[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

An [b]if [/b]statement can include another [b]if[/b] statement to form a nested statement. Nesting an [b]if [/b]allows a decision to be based on further requirements. 
Consider the following statement: [code format="c" codeId="1640"]if (profit > 1000)
  if (clients > 15)
    bonus = 100;
  else
    bonus = 25; [/code]
Appropriately indenting nested statements will help clarify the meaning to a reader. However, be sure to understand that an [b]else [/b]clause is associated with the closest [b]if[/b] unless curly braces { } are used to change the association.
[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [code format="c" codeId="1641"]if (profit > 1000) {
  if (clients > 15)
    bonus = 100;
}
else
  bonus = 25;[/code]
[note]Run the code and see how it works![/note]

